<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>News from Asia-Pacific - Latest headlines and news reports - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage of political, social and geostrategic issues across Asia and the Pacific, including those affecting China, Japan, South Korea, North Korea, India, Pakistan and Australia.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/rss</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:30:22Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Mass burials held in Nepal as bodies wash up after catastrophic flooding</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4d162359e92b64b3f120265d25774e284333274d4a47e8908b04cd649c0dbec3</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:28:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T18:40:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/mass-burials-held-in-nepal-as-bodies-wash-up-after-catastrophic-flooding--58c2aaea3b6b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/mass-burials-held-in-nepal-as-bodies-wash-up-after-catastrophic-flooding" /><summary type="html">Every day, new bodies are recovered in Nepal, but many remain unidentifiable. Several days after the disaster, some are already in an advanced state of decomposition. Morgues in the country's main cities are reaching capacity. Faced with the influx of remains, authorities have begun burying them without formal identification. France 24's special correspondents traveled to Bharatpur, in southern Nepal, to one of these burial sites.</summary></entry><entry><title>After the floods, Nepal works to bury hundreds of washed-up unidentified bodies</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9974c8405d7fc3b7a4d818a3c3d3c7b88e3790ff692480d0fa6d958cc32fcbdb</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:28:52Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T14:08:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/after-the-floods-nepal-works-to-bury-hundreds-of-washed-up-unidentified-bodies--bc87514a0be9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/after-the-floods-nepal-works-to-bury-hundreds-of-washed-up-unidentified-bodies" /><summary type="html">Nepal is burying dozens of bodies in multiple trenches as Nepal’s disaster agency said that 1,003 deaths had been counted there, with 3,916 people missing, including 583 foreign nationals. In its latest update, China reported 16 deaths and 546 missing, including 261 foreigners. Crews faced challenging conditions as they searched unstable terrain and piles of debris. FRANCE 24's Shahzaib Wahlah tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Nepal's rescuers navigate mud-swamped tunnels for hundreds of missing workers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f7dd44a7695793a62bc47c916a036ba8d68e82358850eadddfba427b4581d7fe</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:28:58Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T13:59:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/nepal-s-rescuers-navigate-mud-swamped-tunnels-for-hundreds-of-missing-workers--afd55fd213ec.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/nepal-s-rescuers-navigate-mud-swamped-tunnels-for-hundreds-of-missing-workers" /><summary type="html">The death toll in Nepal has crossed 1,000 from the deadly floods that tore through an area on the border with Tibet on August 26, and nearly 4,000 people remain missing. six days on hopes for survivors are dimming, but rescuers focused on a network of hydropower sites along the Trishuli River are holding out hope. Of the roughly 900 workers missing, some 500 people are believed to be trapped in the tunnels, according to Nepalese authorities.</summary></entry><entry><title>Nepal races to find hundreds stuck in hydropower tunnels following floods</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:44bb0456188799ae6eca7dae87e02b26f2175fc972a9e72e2e54ee372e1f0637</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:30:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T09:53:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/nepal-races-to-find-hundreds-stuck-in-hydropower-tunnels-following-floods--ef327437c75e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/nepal-races-to-find-hundreds-stuck-in-hydropower-tunnels-following-floods" /><summary type="html">More than 1,000 people have been killed in the devastating floods that struck the border between Nepal and Tibet. Authorities have started mass burials for unclaimed bodies while they wait for victims' families to claim them. Meanwhile, rescue operations are underway to rescue hundreds of workers stuck in hydropower tunnels. FRANCE 24's Shahzaib Wahlah tells us more from the Chitwan district in Nepal.</summary></entry><entry><title>Tibetan activists accuse China of underreporting flood death toll</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c312f246bf7139087767fa961974077ca7a9c19e3b41dbefaf039b748e8514a1</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:30:10Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T07:59:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260901-tibetan-activists-accuse-china-of-underreporting-flood-death-toll--3962fa94e61e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260901-tibetan-activists-accuse-china-of-underreporting-flood-death-toll" /><summary type="html">Tibetan exiles and activists have accused China of severely underreporting the death toll from the devastating Himalayan floods along its border with Nepal. Beijing has reported 16 deaths and 546 missing in Tibet so far and the foreign ministry insists that the release of information has been "open, transparent and timely".</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>'Glaciers in Himalayas retreating': Nepal floods triggered by 'glacier collapse &amp; massive landslide'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:57cb70a2d2c8b9736214d8da318f8f1642a96cc2089da82a36d98c7d59ed99c3</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:30:14Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T06:26:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260901-glaciers-in-himalayas-retreating-nepal-floods-triggered-by-glacier-collapse-massive-landsli--b54780004ba1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260901-glaciers-in-himalayas-retreating-nepal-floods-triggered-by-glacier-collapse-massive-landslide" /><summary type="html">Annette Young is pleased to welcome Joseph Shea, Glaciologist and Associate Professor at the University of Northern BC. Shea argues that the catastrophe should be understood as a compound event in which a glacier failure and a massive landslide occurred together. His analysis places the disaster within the broader, well-established transformation of the Himalayas under climate change. As warming changes high-mountain environments, scientists may increasingly need to identify subtle precursors to rare but potentially devastating cascading hazards.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Sea change: Much of the world's economic GDP has moved to the Asia-Pacific region'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1f9a74e979775dc7a1b1bd52474c013e650c4d6dbfea5d9d2d71daa2650720e0</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:30:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T05:22:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260901-sea-change-much-of-the-world-s-economic-gdp-has-moved-to-the-asia-pacific-region-rana-mitte--0e4c1b0f2b67.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260901-sea-change-much-of-the-world-s-economic-gdp-has-moved-to-the-asia-pacific-region-rana-mitter" /><summary type="html">François Picard is pleased to welcome Rana Mitter, historian, author and ST Lee Chair in US-Asia Relations at the Harvard Kennedy School. He discusses the significance of the Shanghai Cooperation Organisation (SCO) as it pertains to the evolution of a changing international system, this as the bloc holds a summit in Kyrgyzstan's capital Bishkek.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Melting Himalayas? Nepal disaster exposes growing risk of glacial flooding</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:374034313254e203223f310abc73ba0aad9dadc56ac21ddd22e73d79216dd04e</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:30:19Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T23:35:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260831-melting-himalayas-nepal-disaster-exposes-growing-risk-of-glacial-flooding--06953269a81c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260831-melting-himalayas-nepal-disaster-exposes-growing-risk-of-glacial-flooding" /><summary type="html">It may well be one of the tragic consequences of global warming. Scientists will tell us whether receding glaciers are to blame for last Wednesday’s ice shelf collapse that triggered a catastrophic flood, cascading down more than 3,000 metres from the Chinese border into Nepal.</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>Nepal-Tibet flood death toll surpasses 1,000</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:61feaf27a24c9285bdbd01688b6488a3d7e3bbc9ef74e97784025227a9b6318d</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:30:22Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T23:34:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260831-glacial-flood-death-toll-surpasses-900-in-nepal-and-tibet--b52676f3d5eb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260831-glacial-flood-death-toll-surpasses-900-in-nepal-and-tibet" /><summary type="html">Rescuers battled mud and debris Monday as the death toll from devastating glacial floods along the China-Nepal border topped 1,000, with nearly 4,500 people still missing. Rescue teams continued a desperate search for survivors as entire communities were swept away.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Nepal disaster: Fake and AI images flood social media as deaths mount</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ae5597333332ace73e0da8966c8163f4d2ae45c31cd438eeff4c058299712168</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:27:22Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T20:00:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/nepal-disaster-fake-and-ai-images-flood-social-media-as-deaths-mount--1d940b31fc6b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/nepal-disaster-fake-and-ai-images-flood-social-media-as-deaths-mount" /><summary type="html">As deadly floods hit the Nepal-China border, social media is being inundated with fake and misleading footage. In Truth or Fake, Vedika Bahl goes through viral videos falsely linked to the disaster, including AI-generated content and old recycled footage from India, Chile and Alaska. Some posts have racked up millions of views online, exploiting the tragedy to drive engagement for easy clicks or further perpetuate conspiracy theories.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>Hundreds feared stuck in hydropower tunnels as flood deaths surpass 950 in Nepal and China</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7b9e4f2619e89165326abef1a477ffe44b0e0a442c42f290ac26374955574821</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:27:22Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T18:34:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/hundreds-feared-stuck-in-hydropower-tunnels-as-flood-deaths-surpass-950-in-nepal-and-china--666c35c75ae1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/hundreds-feared-stuck-in-hydropower-tunnels-as-flood-deaths-surpass-950-in-nepal-and-china" /><summary type="html">Rescuers raced Monday to free hundreds of workers believed to be trapped in tunnels at hydropower sites that were buried in mud by catastrophic flooding on the Nepal-China border, as the death toll climbed and increasingly desperate families searched for missing loved ones. FRANCE 24's Eliza Herbert reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Nepal floods 'unprecedented', requires new 'engineering approaches, risk-sensitive urban planning'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:199bceafabf5447d6a16a2d7f513622ac689ac55a498973017d08871e204c751</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:27:22Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T15:52:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/nepal-floods-unprecedented-requires-new-engineering-approaches-risk-sensitive-urban-planning--f18b77019ec7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/nepal-floods-unprecedented-requires-new-engineering-approaches-risk-sensitive-urban-planning" /><summary type="html">Genie Godula is pleased to welcome Dr. Basanta Raj Adhikari, Director of the Center for Disaster Studies at Tribhuvan University’s Institute of Engineering.  He describes the disaster as an illustration of the limits of conventional prevention in the Himalayas. With flood velocities estimated at 170 to 180 kilometres per hour and hazards ranging from ice and snow avalanches to glacial lake outburst floods, he argues that comprehensive monitoring of Nepal’s exceptionally steep and complex mountain terrain is effectively impossible. Yet Adhikari’s analysis is not fatalistic. Instead, he shifts the emphasis from attempting to predict every extreme event toward risk-informed adaptation. Nepal, he argues, should identify high-risk hotspots through satellite observation, supplement these with ground-based monitoring and early-warning systems, and incorporate that knowledge into risk-sensitive land-use planning.</summary></entry><entry><title>Canberra's zoo treats its residents to personnalised musical therapy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3f18283a1091b5c18fa41cb6e85d5cae9dc4471ed743a3171951bcafd9b700b6</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:27:22Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T15:30:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/canberra-s-zoo-treats-its-residents-to-personnalised-musical-therapy--0d0087f76a83.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/canberra-s-zoo-treats-its-residents-to-personnalised-musical-therapy" /><summary type="html">A music therapist in Australia has been playing for animals at Canberra's zoo for the last five years. It's a relaxing experience for animals and staff alike and the animals all react differently to the music played.</summary></entry><entry><title>Nepal deadly floods: FRANCE 24 report – on the ground with survivors</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2fba8692eb532318b3cae5974cb439838387a457e1170f094020dee1aedad504</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:27:22Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T15:12:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260831-nepal-deadly-floods-france-24-report-_-on-the-ground-with-survivors--b891d1208ba1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260831-nepal-deadly-floods-france-24-report-%E2%80%93-on-the-ground-with-survivors" /><summary type="html">In Nepal, after the deadly flood, another ordeal begins for the survivors: finding shelter, food, and simply the means to survive. While rescue workers continue searching for possible survivors, those who escaped the disaster are trying to rebuild their lives, despite the threat of another flood. FRANCE 24's special correspondents visited Sinchaur in the Nuwako district – one of the villages hit by the flood on August 26.</summary></entry><entry><title>Nepal grapples with destruction and loss in wake of deadly floods</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:80d7d21c7555f693b10c75c39eaba9cddbc9c162d19bc3319641a8e5261942e1</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:27:22Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T13:10:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/nepal-grapples-with-destruction-and-loss-in-wake-of-deadly-floods--17641910cea0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/nepal-grapples-with-destruction-and-loss-in-wake-of-deadly-floods" /><summary type="html">Authorities in Nepal have warned of possible fresh flooding after water levels rose in the Bhotekoshi River. The floods took place after a glacier collapse. They have killed at least 900 people - with more than 4,000 others missing in Nepal and Tibet. Now, a massive rescue effort continues and communities grapple with devastation and loss.</summary></entry><entry><title>Nepal races to find its missing as flood area remains largely inaccessible</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:340dc44fed67beb7bd85eb11a4005cb17e9ec1a1d6d0d04b435a760c3075f4b7</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:27:22Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T12:41:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/nepal-races-to-find-its-missing-as-flood-area-remains-largely-inaccessible--450be663b9f0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/nepal-races-to-find-its-missing-as-flood-area-remains-largely-inaccessible" /><summary type="html">Nepal's rescuers are racing against the clock to find the over 4,000 people missing after the flash floods that devastated an area in the north of the country on August 26. Rescue operations include one where workers are trying to save hundreds believed to be stuck inside a blocked hydropower project. Meanwhile, authorities have started burying unclaimed bodies. FRANCE 24's Shahzaib Wahlah tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>After the floods, Nepal's survivors look to rebuilding their lives</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a2f9055c1a88f99f0c484e56cf2f063cde8beb4a7e02f54f8949ad371f271a3f</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:27:22Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T10:53:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/after-the-floods-nepal-s-survivors-look-to-rebuilding-their-lives--e039613e514e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/after-the-floods-nepal-s-survivors-look-to-rebuilding-their-lives" /><summary type="html">In Nepal, after the deadly flood, another ordeal begins for the survivors: finding shelter, food, and simply the means to survive. In the devastated villages, families lost everything in minutes. And while rescue workers continue searching for possible survivors, those who escaped the disaster are trying to rebuild their lives, despite the threat of another flood. FRANCE 24's special correspondents visited Sinchaur, in the Nuwako district, one of the villages hit by the flood of August 26.</summary></entry><entry><title>Nepal starts burying its dead as search for over 4,200 missing continues</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:225bba5f94e8004a7d2864c7b9c9d2f0a868e6fedec57f9723455da8dafaaea2</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:27:22Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T10:33:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/nepal-starts-burying-its-dead-as-search-for-over-4-200-missing-continues--d8984474f7d9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/nepal-starts-burying-its-dead-as-search-for-over-4-200-missing-continues" /><summary type="html">The combined deaths in Nepal and China surpassed 900, with more than 4,700 people missing. It also includes 933 workers on hydropower projects along the river which the torrent crashed through. With morgues running at full capacity, the country has started to bury unclaimed bodies. FRANCE 244s Shazaib Wahlah tells us more from a grief-stricken Nepal.</summary></entry><entry><title>What to know about the SCO, the summit billed as a counterweight to US influence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b2e5690809bc9df4498034c525292945d9f553b9c26afbcfcaa4ed7883f1e941</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:27:22Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T10:31:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/what-to-know-about-the-sco-the-summit-billed-as-a-counterweight-to-us-influence--bcde7c336260.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/what-to-know-about-the-sco-the-summit-billed-as-a-counterweight-to-us-influence" /><summary type="html">The leaders of China, Russia and India are among the heads of state gathering in Kyrgyzstan for the summit of the Shanghai Cooperation Organization. The summit is celebrating its 25 years in existence. Although the group is billed as a counterweight to US. global influence, it is not the case for all participating countries. FRANCE 24's Oliver Farry takes a look at what the SCO is, and what will be discussed this year.</summary></entry><entry><title>Nepal rescue teams seek hundreds of workers trapped in hydropower tunnels by deadly floods</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aec8fde555d402e5ea0f95166437decdb43add904598935be2bb0b7cecc3bd68</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:27:22Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T09:15:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260831-nepal-rescue-teams-seek-hundreds-of-workers-trapped-in-hydropower-tunnels-by-deadly-floods--361362dcb3af.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260831-nepal-rescue-teams-seek-hundreds-of-workers-trapped-in-hydropower-tunnels-by-deadly-floods" /><summary type="html">Supported by experts from China and India, Nepal's rescue teams on Monday endeavoured to reach hundreds of workers believed to be trapped in hydropower tunnels blocked by the devastating flood of mud, water and debris that swept through the Himalayan region last week.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>What justice for Nepal after flooding?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:76a2d7ca7b6ecd68815586f461bd4b5ab087dac0742766cf19ba3075868bad99</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:27:22Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T07:54:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20260831-what-justice-for-nepal--ce44c0b4ecf3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20260831-what-justice-for-nepal" /><summary type="html">PRESS REVIEW – Monday, August 31: The international press tell the story of a heroic headmaster in Nepal who managed to save more than 1,600 pupils, while the Nepali press lambast a lack of accountability for major polluters. Meanwhile in France, back-to-school season reopens wounds over child sex abuse in before- and after-school clubs. Finally, do ants and bees have a concept of voting?</summary><category term="Press Review" /></entry><entry><title>Nepal buries victims of Himalayan flooding as death toll climbs past 900</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:59ec3c432fd5a9675e4982e118e2537c011a909a3dad29aa3d83a0446a218dea</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:27:22Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T05:46:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260831-nepal-buries-victims-of-himalayan-flooding-as-death-toll-climbs-past-900--38c4dbe0877d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260831-nepal-buries-victims-of-himalayan-flooding-as-death-toll-climbs-past-900" /><summary type="html">Nepal on Monday began mass burials for the hundreds of people killed in catastrophic flash floods along the Nepal-Tibet border last week, as authorities announced the death toll had climbed past 900 people. Officials in Nepal and neighbouring China are still searching for more than 4,000 missing people, including hundreds of hydropower plant workers across the remote Himalayan region.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Putin and Xi rally allies at Kyrgyzstan summit to counter US influence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a3166e6f0d3b5d74412602e98dacc6cab4bc688d172b48abd402fc5999ab9c33</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:27:22Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T02:09:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260831-putin-and-xi-rally-allies-at-kyrgyzstan-summit-to-counter-us-influence--95bc6b506cc0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260831-putin-and-xi-rally-allies-at-kyrgyzstan-summit-to-counter-us-influence" /><summary type="html">Leaders from more than a dozen countries, including Russia's Vladimir Putin, China's Xi Jinping, India's Narendra Modi and Iran's Masoud Pezeshkian, gathered in Kyrgyzstan on Monday for the summit of the Shanghai Cooperation Organisation, a group billed as a counterweight to US influence.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Week in pictures: devastating floods in Nepal, death of Dolly Parton and a tornado in France</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:56220648c818b91c27020fbb77452f1c4e4f9e93b26e747a4d17886790b992bc</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:27:22Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T14:47:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260830-week-in-pictures-devastating-floods-in-nepal-death-of-dolly-parton-and-a-tornado-in-france--6e7418132498.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260830-week-in-pictures-devastating-floods-in-nepal-death-of-dolly-parton-and-a-tornado-in-france" /><summary type="html">A look back at some of the week's key news stories and the most striking images: a devastating flood tears through Nepal and Tibet, the death of global icon Dolly Parton, a tornado devastates a village in southern France and the Humanoid Robot World Games in China offers a peek at the future.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Nepal: Thousands still missing as death toll rises</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2c992b4078b818231dd0532014f0ccdf608b111fc2f8871be0137ffb59214266</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:27:22Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T10:04:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/nepal-thousands-still-missing-as-death-toll-rises--19b14e275677.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/nepal-thousands-still-missing-as-death-toll-rises" /><summary type="html">Nepalese authorities announced on Sunday that the provisional death toll from the devastating floods had risen to more than 730, with nearly 2,500 people still missing.

Among the thousands of people missing is the husband of a 22-year-old woman, who is still waiting for him to return. Like tens of thousands of Nepalese people in recent days, she went to one of the country’s medical centres to find out whether her husband was among those whose bodies had been recovered in recent days. Caitlin Brown reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Nepal: Glacial collapse leaves 3,000 missing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b09a025583b7d3b5da31db5dd632af856ebf23b55ce9891d054bf165a7aa5670</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:27:22Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T09:16:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/nepal-glacial-collapse-leaves-3-000-missing--bf2b04c1f945.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/nepal-glacial-collapse-leaves-3-000-missing" /><summary type="html">Rescue and relief efforts in Nepal and Tibet have been hampered this Sunday by heavy rain and rising river levels. The latest figures following Wednesday’s flash floods put the death toll at 750, while more than 3,000 people remain missing. Nepal’s disaster authorities are urging rescue teams to “exercise caution”, warning that bad weather, swollen rivers and the threat of further flooding could hamper operations. Shazab Wahlah reports from the town of Bidur.</summary></entry><entry><title>Death toll rises as 3,000 remain missing in Nepal, China</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dc534c9e31271f2e8e55f343a9c8aa452751ee154ed6bdc6416c0b20d4b9ed9a</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:27:22Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T08:37:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/death-toll-rises-as-3-000-remain-missing-in-nepal-china--6a7e3695e252.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/death-toll-rises-as-3-000-remain-missing-in-nepal-china" /><summary type="html">Rescue and relief efforts in Nepal and Tibet have been hampered this Sunday by heavy rain and rising river levels. The latest figures following Wednesday’s flash floods put the death toll at 750, while more than 3,000 people remain missing. Nepal’s disaster authorities are urging rescue teams to “exercise caution”, warning that bad weather, swollen rivers and the threat of further flooding could hamper operations. Shazab Wahlah reports from the town of Bidur.</summary></entry><entry><title>Putin, Xi set for Central Asia summit as Russia and China seek to counter Western influence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d70b2cc4e6b9c10c30a0eb7f94efaecb4463eae58cdd5575a78863baccbf400f</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:27:22Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T05:51:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260830-putin-xi-set-for-central-asia-summit-as-russia-china-seek-to-counter-western-influence--62e15ee5debd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260830-putin-xi-set-for-central-asia-summit-as-russia-china-seek-to-counter-western-influence" /><summary type="html">Russian President Vladimir Putin and Chinese President Xi Jinping are due in Kyrgyzstan on Monday for a two-day summit, joined by the leaders of Iran and India. The gathering comes as the group seeks to project a united front amid wars in Ukraine and Iran and growing tensions with the West.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Nepal begins mass burials as flood death toll surpasses 780</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e65c1a0e9457dba467316a05114784462e3c8a760c2db8acf491f2fad676d5b0</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:27:22Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T04:59:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260830-nepal-tibet-floods-live-at-least-750-dead-as-death-toll-rises--8e74f89e9cff.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260830-nepal-tibet-floods-live-at-least-750-dead-as-death-toll-rises" /><summary type="html">Nepal on Sunday began temporarily burying some of the hundreds of bodies recovered from devastating floods after taking DNA samples and marking the remains so families can identify and retrieve them later. Rescue efforts entered a fifth day, with heavy overnight rain and rising rivers hampering attempts to reach hydropower workers believed to be trapped in tunnels. Read our blog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Missing toll from Nepal, China flood nears 3,000 as race for survivors continues</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b01f596c8cfdfb9323577434e403bd8bc051b644e7489dcb7a40ca6bfc64a8a6</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:27:22Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T20:12:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260829-missing-toll-from-nepal-china-flood-nears-3-000-as-race-for-survivors-continues--011d0bbdf6ff.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260829-missing-toll-from-nepal-china-flood-nears-3-000-as-race-for-survivors-continues" /><summary type="html">Rescuers in Nepal and China on Saturday continued to search for the nearly 3,000 people missing after devastating flooding along the border with China engulfed entire villages earlier this week. At least 682 bodies were recovered in both countries, including 675 in Nepal and seven in China.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry></feed>
